From 67d3125a2b161e42bd57ae5b86d1020f55d23027 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: J P <jpwatters@mac.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 18:31:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 04/30] network-radio: full-rate NAS stream on the Tab5 - WiFi
 RX fixes, build on macOS

Bring-up on the real hardware (Tab5 + QMX+ on a Synology DS416j) found the
Tab5's WiFi receive path, not the relay, limiting the stream to 10-20k of
48k I/Q pairs/s and starving touch input. Now 47.7k pairs/s with touch working.

esp_hosted SDIO RX (two new standing patches, both in check_patches.py):
- apply_esp_hosted_sdio_split_bundles.ps1 (QMX_SDIO_RX_SPLIT): the C6 streams
  several frames per SDIO read; only the first survived a normal read and a
  burst was drained and discarded whole. Every frame is now split out into
  its own mempool buffer and delivered.
- apply_esp_hosted_sdio_rx_copy_psram.ps1 (QMX_SDIO_RX_COPY_PSRAM): every
  received frame was copied into internal RAM (malloc under
  SPIRAM_MALLOC_ALWAYSINTERNAL) and held until TCP delivered it, exhausting
  internal/DMA RAM under a sustained stream (touch and web server stopped).
  The copy now goes to PSRAM; allocation failure drops the frame, no assert.
- sdkconfig: LWIP TCP receive window 2880 -> 11520, recvmbox 6 -> 12
  (send buffer stays 2880).

Firmware:
- radio_relay: no lwIP call before WiFi is up (boot loop: getaddrinfo on a
  tcpip stack that did not exist yet asserted in cat_link at 4 s).
- PROJECT_VER = latest tag + "-NAS" (e.g. v1.16.11-NAS).
- idf_component.yml: pin cdc_acm 2.4.0, usb_host_hid 1.2.0, esp_codec_dev
  1.5.11, mdns 1.11.3 - the versions in the official v1.16.11 image; a fresh
  fetch of newer ones built without working touch.
- apply_cdc_acm_close_tolerant.ps1 also accepts cdc_acm 2.4.1;
  apply_httpd_ws_dead_socket_close.ps1 matches LF as well as CRLF trees.

NAS relay: CAT/terminal frames are sent before queued I/Q, the I/Q queue is
3 frames and the kernel send buffer 8 KB, so a slow link drops I/Q instead of
delaying CAT (IQ-mode setup timed out before). check.sh restarts the relay on
request (restart.request file), finding it via /proc.

macOS tools: tools/mac-build-flash.sh (PowerShell patches, ESP-IDF env with
PlatformIO's python kept out, build, flash) and tools/mac-capture-serial.sh.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01W7MAsxUnuCnfwkHxdqp61S
